  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Cuerpo:** *head, eye, ear, nose, mouth, tooth (teeth), throat, neck, shoulder, arm, hand, finger, back, stomach, leg, knee, foot (feet)*.",
      "",
      "**Plurales irregulares:** *tooth → teeth · foot → feet*.",
      "",
      "**Decir que algo duele**",
      "",
      "- **My + parte + hurts**: *My back hurts.* (plural: *My legs hurt.*)",
      "- **I've got a + dolencia**: *a headache, a toothache, a cold, a cough, a fever, a sore throat.*",
      "- **I've got a pain in my** + parte: *I've got a pain in my chest.*",
      "",
      "**Ojo, falso amigo:** *constipated* significa **estreñido**, no resfriado. 'Estoy resfriado' = *I've got a cold.*",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *stomach* /ˈstʌmək/ (la ch suena /k/) · *throat* /θrəʊt/ · *cough* /kɒf/ (rima con *off*) · *headache* /ˈhedeɪk/."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "I am constipated.",
        "right": "I've got a cold.",
        "note": "Constipated significa estreñido."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "I have pain in the head.",
        "right": "I've got a headache.",
        "note": "Para la cabeza se usa headache."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": [
      {
        "word": "constipated",
        "es_false": "constipado (resfriado)",
        "real": "estreñido",
        "note": "Resfriado se dice have a cold."
      }
    ]
  },
